=== PROOF SUMMARY (Milestone 2) =====================================
Target: LoadApp pid=4043 (-Xmx256m -XX:+UseG1GC, Temurin 21.0.13), same
workload and flags as proof/run1.log. Appraan run: 30 s, interval 5 s,
web UI on the default port 7676 (startup line at the top of this log).

PROOF PATH — fallback ladder, rung 1 (live HTTP via curl) WORKED:
  All seven routes were fetched with curl from the *live* server mid-run
  and returned HTTP 200: / (6709 B), /flame (14261 B), /api/summary,
  /api/gc, /api/cpu, /api/cores, /api/stacks. Bodies are saved in
  proof/run2/ with the -live suffix.
  Rung 2 (in-process java.net.http.HttpClient, see RenderProof section
  above) is BLOCKED by this sandbox's network policy — the client
  connection is intercepted ("Other TCP connections is turned off for
  this assistant") before it reaches the server. curl, not being a Java
  process, is unaffected. So live HTTP serving is verified by real
  external fetches; the Java-client failure is a sandbox policy artefact,
  reported here rather than hidden. RenderProof additionally rendered
  every artefact through the same pure functions the handlers delegate
  to (proof/run2/ without the -live suffix) from its own live 15 s
  pipeline session against the same target.

CONSISTENCY — the curl-fetched payloads and the console block printed
from the same snapshot agree EXACTLY:
  console: young=17 old=0 pause=34ms/3ms lastYoung=174ms ago;
           alloc total=825.5 MiB rate=161.4 MiB/s heap=7.0 MiB (2213 events);
           samples=728, isPrime=707, churnAllocations=8, ArrayList.clear=6;
